[48.812855, "o", "  ⚙ bash pip3 --version\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  glimmer-30b — 19 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 install --dry-run wheel — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 install --dry-run wheel\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  glimmer-30b — 20 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 install --quiet --upgrade pip — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 install --quiet --upgrade pip\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  glimmer-30b — 21 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 --version — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 --version\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  glimmer-30b — 22 tool call(s) so far\r\n  glimmer-30b — 23 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ note \r\n    ✓ note — pip package files missing but pip-24.3.1.dist-info remained,\r\nYour system Python 3.13 had a broken pip install: the package files were missing but `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` remained in `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages`. Because of that `ensurepip` thought pip was already satisfied and never re-installed the code, so `import pip` failed with `ModuleNotFoundError`."]
[48.812883, "o", "\r\n\r\nI removed the stale metadata and forced a reinstall:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nrm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info\r\npython3 -m ensurepip --default-pip\r\n```\r\n\r\nCheck:\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ python3 -c \"import pip; print(pip.__file__)\"\r\n/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip/__init__.py\r\n\r\n$ pip3 --version\r\npip 26.3 from /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip (python 3.13)\r\n```\r\n\r\n`pip3 install` now works end-to-end. I also upgraded pip to 26.3. If you want to avoid this in the future, prefer virtual environments for project installs; system pip is fragile when files are removed manually.\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=glimmer-30b tools=23 surface=a148f33da19b\r\n"]
